.TH BURNREPORT 1 "2026-08-05" "Burn Suite 1.0" "Burn Suite Manual"
.SH NAME
burnreport \- cross\-tool report combiner for the Burn Suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 ./burnreport.py
.br
.B burnreport
.RI ( "if installed via " install.sh )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B burnreport
does not scan anything itself. It reads the existing \fB.txt\fR
reports already sitting in \fIburn_report/\fR (written by
.BR burnscanner (1),
.BR burncracker (1),
.BR burnrecon (1),
and
.BR burnweb (1) ),
lets you pick several to combine, and merges their findings and
diagnostics into one summarized report \- with each entry tagged by
which tool it came from, sorted by severity.
.PP
Useful when an engagement touched the same target with multiple tools
and you want one document instead of several. Does not require root.
.SH USAGE
.TP
.B 1.
Run with no arguments. Every report found in \fIburn_report/\fR is
listed, newest first, showing its source tool, parsed target, and
timestamp.
.TP
.B 2.
Enter a comma\-separated list of report numbers to combine, or type
.B all
to combine everything listed.
.TP
.B 3.
A combined report is written to
\fIburn_report/burnreport_<timestamp>.txt\fR containing:
.RS
.IP \(bu 3
.B SOURCE REPORTS
\- which reports were combined
.IP \(bu 3
.B COMBINED FINDINGS
\- every finding from every source, tagged with its source tool and
sorted by severity
.IP \(bu 3
.B COMBINED DIAGNOSTICS
\- every diagnostic code from every source, tagged with its source tool
.RE
.SH PARSING NOTES
The combiner parses
.B burnscanner ,
.B burnrecon ,
and
.B burnweb
reports' structured \fBFINDINGS SUMMARY\fR / \fBVULNERABILITY SUMMARY\fR
sections directly \- these three tools share one format by design so
they combine cleanly.
.B burncracker
reports have a different shape (a single pass/fail result, not a
findings list) and are included for their target/DIAGNOSTICS
information but don't contribute to the findings list.
.PP
This is not a general\-purpose report parser \- it expects the exact
format the other four tools write. If you hand\-edit a report file
before combining, keep the section headers and \fB[SEVERITY] Title\fR
/ \fBFIX \->\fR structure intact.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Completed normally.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid or empty selection.
.TP
.B 3
No reports found in \fIburn_report/\fR to combine.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Logs its own failures as \fBREPORT\-NNN\fR codes \- see
.I ERROR_CODES.txt
in the suite root.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I burn_report/burnreport_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.txt
Generated combined report for each run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR burnscanner (1),
.BR burncracker (1),
.BR burnrecon (1),
.BR burnweb (1),
.BR burnsuite (7)
